# Typing "/" in the composer raises the command menu, and a slash command is
# carried out by the client instead of being sent to the agent as text.
#
# The rows are asserted by their blurbs, not by the verb: "/model" is also what
# the field itself holds, so asserting the word would pass on the typed text
# alone with no menu on screen at all.
#
# The script never clicks the field twice in quick succession. Two clicks a few
# frames apart are a DOUBLE click when the frames are fast, and that window is
# real time — the first version of this test re-clicked to select the draft and
# retype it, which passed only while the machine was loaded and failed on an
# idle one. So the draft is grown by typing onto what is already there, and the
# one place it has to be emptied uses the app's own Esc-to-clear. (select_all
# is no help: the harness cannot hold Super, gap #49.)
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

expect_text "needs a decision"

click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4

# A bare slash offers the whole vocabulary.
type "/"
wait_frames 8
expect_text "start a new conversation"
expect_text "compact the context now"

# Typing on narrows it to one command.
type "mod"
wait_frames 8
expect_text "switch the model"
expect_no_text "compact the context now"

# Clicking a row that takes an argument completes the verb into the field and
# leaves the caret there, so the argument can be typed straight away.
click_ui slash_item_0
wait_frames 8
type "opus"
wait_frames 8
expect_input_text composer_reply_input "/model opus"

# Return runs it. There is no model picker in this client yet, so the strip
# says so — and the words never reach the agent as a message.
key ENTER
wait_frames 20
expect_text "no model picker yet"
expect_input_text composer_reply_input "/model opus"

# Esc putting the MENU away without clearing the draft has its own script
# (slash_menu_escape_keeps_draft.e2e) — here the menu is already closed, so Esc
# means the field's clear, which is what the /new phase needs.
#
# /new is the one verb with somewhere to go: it raises the new-conversation
# sheet. Esc on a focused field is the app's clear (escape_system.h resolves it
# to the transcript once no menu is up); it blurs the field on the way out,
# which is afterhours' own behaviour (gap #57), so the caret is clicked back —
# and by then the field is empty, so what that click selects cannot matter.
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 6
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
type "/new"
wait_frames 8
key ENTER
wait_frames 20
expect_text "Describe the task"
